Design notes:

- The unit of work is created with the SObject types in dependency order (Account before Contact), so the parent is inserted first.
- `registerNew(contact, Contact.AccountId, account)` records the relationship. At commit, fflib resolves the Account Id into `AccountId`.
- A single `commitWork()` performs one insert per SObject type, which keeps it bulk-safe.
- Null or empty input returns an empty list before any unit of work is created, so nothing is written.
- Null or blank account names, and null or blank last names, are not handled specially, because the task doesn't specify that. I skip null or blank last names so the commit doesn't fail on a required field, and I let a blank account name fail naturally, since Account Name is required and failing loudly is clearer than silently dropping the account.
- The class uses `with sharing`, which is the safe default.

